  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlas Air recorded $565M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Atlas Air received 339 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.7M. Atlas Air's obligations are down 25.6% year over year. Atlas Air concentrated most of FY2026 obligations in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which totaled $563M, while Scheduled Freight Air Transportation totaled $1.1M and smaller services such as Other Technical and Trade Schools and Flight Training recorded $333K and $332K respectively. Atlas Air's fiscal-year history shows $759M in obligations for FY25 and $565M for FY26, compared with lower totals in earlier years: $13.5M in FY21, $1.7M in FY22, $6M in FY23, and $3.7M in FY24. The current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date, and the largest contract values in market tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Atlas Air's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Atlas Air concentrated FY2026 obligations in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which totaled $563M. Atlas Air recorded $1.1M in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation and small amounts in Other Technical and Trade Schools and Flight Training, $333K and $332K respectively. Atlas Air's concentration means most FY2026 obligations were in passenger charter services rather than a broad spread of markets."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Atlas Air's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Atlas Air's obligations fell 25.6% year over year. Atlas Air recorded $759M in FY25 and $565M in FY26 to date, after smaller totals in prior years: $13.5M in FY21, $1.7M in FY22, $6M in FY23, and $3.7M in FY24. Atlas Air's FY2026 figures are fiscal year to date and partial for the current year."
      }
    ]
  },
